      "final_text": "Done \u2014 `check_candidate` returns `VERIFIED` and the passport reproduces.\n\nWhat changed (only [candidate/Solution.lean](<workspace>/candidate/Solution.lean)):\n- `VyperSqrt.sqrt` is now the deployed loop with the PR 4486 fix: `vyperSqrtWith (fun y z => if y < z then y else z)` (minimum of the last two iterates) instead of returning the last iterate.\n- A `master` lemma proves this computes `Nat.sqrt (a * 10^10)` for positive decimals: the Nat trajectory stays in range and above the root, halves its error each step (error \u2264 2 after 168 steps via a closed-form bound), lands in `{root, root+1}` by step 169, and the integer loop tracks the Nat loop (early stops are exact fixed points, handled separately, including the `seed = a` edge case). The three hard theorems follow from the root's bounds; neg-reverts and deployed-loop are direct.\n\nVerification observed: `lean_build` clean with no `sorry`; `check_candidate` VERIFIED on all 5 requirements across all six kernels with permitted axioms only, executable passing 2001 property cases; `verify_passport` reproduced (`passport-002.json`, sha256 `6537e87c\u2026`).",
